    <summary>Awesome web server for Windows</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[nginx [engine x] is an HTTP and reverse proxy server, a mail proxy server, and a generic TCP/UDP proxy server, originally written by Igor Sysoev.
This package provides an `nssm` Windows service wrapper for it which creates a standard Windows
service named `nginx` to manage the server.

#### N!B! This repository lists both nginx versions - stable and mainline:

* **Stable** and **mainline** only differ by version numbers. On command `choco install nginx-service` the stable will be installed. To access mainline version, you must use pre-release `--pre` switch or specify exact version number, which has `-mainline` appended to it.
* **Mainline** version might contain more edge features, whereas **stable** will be more prone to bugs. Both versions should receive critical security fixes. If you use this package for development and need to access latest features, go for mainline. If deployment is for longterm and unattended stability - choose stable.
* More info on [different nginx versions](https://www.nginx.com/blog/nginx-1-6-1-7-released/)

During installation `nginx-service` will create following directory structure:
```
C:/tools/nginx/
├── conf
│   ├── nginx.original.conf {conf file shipped with official .zip}
│   ├── nginx.conf          {tailored version of above file}
│   └── ...
├── conf.d
│   └── server.default.conf
├── html
│   └── index.html
├── logs
│   └── {Required}
└── temp
    └── {Required}
```

* Place your custom config files inside `conf.d`
* Conf to be included must follow naming pattern `server*.conf` where `*` is a wildcard
* Above allows config pattern where extra `.conf` files are included (and reused) manually from `server*.conf`, i.e. PHP location directive
* It is safe to edit/rename/remove default config files. They will be restored during upgrade only if `conf.d` is empty

Afterwards, you can start and stop the service with following commands: `nssm start nginx-service` and `nssm stop nginx-service`
On default, the service will autostart with Windows. To disable this use Services GUI console.

See the [nginx.org](https://nginx.org) for more detailed documentation.
]]></description>
	<releaseNotes><![CDATA[*) Security: a buffer overflow might occur in a worker process when
   using the "alias" directive if the request URI was changed by the
   "rewrite" directive and was then mapped to a file path
   (CVE-2026-15176).

*) Security: a buffer overflow might occur in a worker process while
   evaluating string expressions with variables, which affected the
   document root calculation and request logging in the http and stream
   modules (CVE-2026-93479).
   Thanks to Matt Suiche of Tolmo Inc.

*) Security: when using HTTP/3 a part of an unknown frame might be
   treated as the request body, which might result in bypassing the
   "client_max_body_size" limit or injecting data in the proxied request
   (CVE-2026-95101).
   Thanks to Hansol Lee of GOTROOT.

*) Security: when using TLS session ticket key rotation, one of the keys
   was left uninitialized, which might allow to forge a session
   (CVE-2026-97629).
   Thanks to PhiNode Labs.

*) Security: when using asynchronous file I/O (AIO), use-after-free
   might occur in certain configurations if the SSI page has "include
   virtual" commands (CVE-2026-97205).
   Thanks to cyberlancer.

*) Feature: the ngx_http_geoip_module and ngx_stream_geoip_module now
   support databases in the MaxMind DB (MMDB) format.

*) Feature: now backend SSL certificates can be verified by IP address.
   Thanks to Maxim Dounin.

*) Feature: now QUIC supports reconfiguration and binary upgrade when
   using the "quic_bpf" directive.

*) Change: the ngx_http_v2_module now uses the RFC 9218 prioritization
   scheme, and RFC 7540 priority signals are ignored.

*) Bugfix: a segmentation fault might occur in a worker process or
   "request count is zero" alerts might appear in logs if the
   "X-Accel-Redirect" header line was cached and the cached response was
   then served to a client.
   Thanks to JiÅ™Ã­ SetniÄka and Maxim Dounin.

*) Bugfix: a segmentation fault might occur in a worker process if the
   ngx_http_dav_module was used to handle COPY and MOVE methods in a
   location with the "alias" directive.
   Thanks to Maxim Dounin.

*) Bugfix: QUIC connections might be closed with the "quic flood
   detected" message in logs if the "http3_stream_buffer_size" directive
   was set to a small value; the bug had appeared in 1.27.5.

*) Bugfix: closing an SSL connection without close_notify was treated as
   a clean shutdown, including the case when the connection was reset;
   now "SSL_read() failed" errors appear in logs in this case.
   Thanks to Maxim Dounin.

*) Bugfix: "[crit] SSL_write() failed" messages might appear in logs
   when an error occurred while reading from an SSL connection.]]></releaseNotes>
    <dependencies>
		  <dependency id="nssm" version="2.24.0" />
    </dependencies>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <file src="bin\**" target="bin" />
    <file src="tools\**" target="tools" />
  </files>
</package>
